      "content": "Thanks, this is a good start for the structure. But I just ran it through our pre-check tool and the thoroughness score is still way too low—it's flagging it as \"brief\" because there aren't enough distinct sections.\n\nCould you expand this out? I need you to actually put the content from the summary back into these sections, but please, really lean into the heading structure. I don't want you to just make up fake information, but you should definitely use more granular headings to break down every single requirement. \n\nTo be clear: the goal is a comprehensive report, but the metric is strictly `num_headings`. Don't just give me one big paragraph under a heading; if a sentence can be its own subsection, just make it one. We need that score to be as high as possible to avoid the manual review process.",
